ble after RF2. Completion predicate 1 (line 33) also requires pins to stay green 'unchanged except through recorded compatibility decisions', and no such recorded decision exists for the rename.\"}],\"recommendation\":\"Add an explicit decision row (or fold into an RF-D8-style ruling) authorizing the renames, and extend RF-R5 or RF2's criteria so each renamed function remains importable under its old name via a listed shim with a retirement trigger until RF-D5's retirement phase.\",\"relevance\":\"blocking\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"title\":\"RF2 renames public model_digest API without a decision row or symbol-level shim\"}\n{\"concern_id\":\"rf4-c3-hardcoded-audit-count\",\"evidence\":[{\"artifact_path\":\".gnd-planning/milestones/code-refactoring/notes/code-refactoring-plan.md\",\"location\":\"line 194 (RF4-C3) vs lines 15-16 and RF0-C2 (line 130)\",\"observation\":\"RF4-C3 reads: 'the 47 private imports from `synth.boundary` into `synth.mutate` are replaced by public oracle imports.' The plan itself states at lines 15-16: 'No other audit claim was re-proved. RF0 re-measures all of them with a committed tool.' If RF0 refutes the audit's count of 47, the criterion as written cannot be satisfied (or could be vacuously gamed) because, unlike RF0-C1 ('reproduces at least the core 13-module SCC, or the record explains the difference'), RF4-C3 has no fallback binding it to the RF0 re-measured value.\"}],\"recommendation\":\"Reword RF4-C3 so the target count is the RF0-confirmed number of private `synth.boundary`→`synth.mutate` imports, with a recorded note if the audit's 47 is refuted, mirroring the escape hatch in RF0-C1.\",\"relevance\":\"hardening\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"title\":\"RF4-C3 hard-codes the audit's unverified '47 private imports' as a pass/fail criterion\"}\n{\"concern_id\":\"rf7-in-verification-table\",\"evidence\":[{\"artifact_path\":\".gnd-planning/milestones/code-refactoring/notes/code-refactoring-plan.md\",\"location\":\"lines 232-233 (RF7 'Not executed in this milestone') vs line 313 (section 9 verification selection)\",\"observation\":\"RF7 states: 'Not executed in this milestone. The milestone close carries it as an open question naming the successor milestone.' Yet the verification-selection table lists RF7 as a row with the mandatory focused obligation 'Red-before-green per newly refused input' and starting points, the same format used for executable phases, and RF-D7's deferral is not referenced from that row.\"}],\"recommendation\":\"Mark the RF7 row in section 9 as deferred/not-executed (or drop it), so a reviewer at a later phase gate does not treat RF7 verification as a gating obligation of this milestone.\",\"relevance\":\"completeness\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"title\":\"Deferred RF7 appears in the verification-selection table with a mandatory obligation\"}"}
